-- title:
--   Linear forms in selected variables, Vandermonde block forms, factor choices and mixed polynomials
-- statement:
--   This module provides the linear-form and counting vocabulary used to compare graded pieces of quotients by products of linear forms with coefficients of a product of binomials. Throughout, $K$ is a field and $K[x]=K[x_v:v\in\sigma]$ is a polynomial ring.
--
--   1. **Linear forms in selected variables.** For a finite index set $\tau$ and a map $v:\tau\to\sigma$ selecting variables, $\Lambda_v:K^{\tau}\to K[x]$ is the $K$-linear map
--   $$
--   \Lambda_v(c)=\sum_{t\in\tau}c_t\,x_{v(t)} .
--   $$
--
--   2. **Linear coefficient subspace.** For an ideal $I\subseteq K[x]$, $W_v(I)=\{c\in K^{\tau}:\Lambda_v(c)\in I\}$ is the subspace of coefficient vectors of those linear forms in the selected variables that belong to $I$.
--
--   3. **Block variables.** For a finite set $\iota$ and $a:\iota\to\mathbb N$, the variable set is $\{(j,h): j\in\iota,\ 0\le h\le a_j\}$. Block $j$ consists of the $a_j+1$ variables $x_{j,0},\dots,x_{j,a_j}$ (homogeneous coordinates on $\mathbb P^{a_j}$), and the block of $x_{j,h}$ is $j$.
--
--   4. **Vandermonde block forms.** For a block $j$ and $t\in K$,
--   $$
--   \ell_j(t)=\sum_{h=0}^{a_j}t^{h}\,x_{j,h},
--   $$
--   the linear form in block $j$ whose coefficient vector is the moment vector $(1,t,\dots,t^{a_j})$. It is multihomogeneous of multidegree $\mathbf e_j$ for the block multigrading, in which every variable of block $j$ has weight the unit vector $\mathbf e_j\in\mathbb Z^{\iota}$.
--
--   5. **Piece dimensions.** For a weight $w:\sigma\to G$ into an additive abelian group, an ideal $I$ and $d\in G$, $\operatorname{pd}(I,d)=\dim_K P_d/(I\cap P_d)$, where $P_d$ is the space of polynomials all of whose monomials have weight $d$.
--
--   6. **Factor choices.** Let $q_1,\dots,q_m$ be a list of factor pairs $q_k=(a_k,b_k,e_{a_k},e_{b_k})$, i.e. polynomials $a_k,b_k$ that are $w$-homogeneous of the recorded degrees $e_{a_k},e_{b_k}\in G$. For a choice vector $c\in\{0,1\}^m$, the choice ideal is generated by $b_k$ for the indices with $c_k=1$ and by $a_k$ for the indices with $c_k=0$ (the zero ideal if $m=0$), and the choice shift is $\sum_{k:\,c_k=1}e_{a_k}\in G$.
--
--   7. **Choice counts and mixed polynomials.** For a finite set $E$ and maps $g,u,v:E\to\iota$, the choice count of $g$ is the vector $\bigl(\#\{e\in E: g(e)=j\}\bigr)_{j\in\iota}\in\mathbb N^{\iota}$, and the mixed polynomial is
--   $$
--   M_{u,v}=\prod_{e\in E}\bigl(X_{u(e)}+X_{v(e)}\bigr)\in\mathbb N[X_j: j\in\iota].
--   $$
--   Expanding the product, the coefficient of $X^{a}$ in $M_{u,v}$ is the number of ways to choose, for every $e\in E$, one of $u(e)$ and $v(e)$ so that the choice count of the chosen labels equals $a$.
--
--   8. **Ideal maps in a fixed degree.** If $F_i$ is $w$-homogeneous of degree $e_i$ for each $i$ in a finite set $E$, the $K$-linear map
--   $$
--   \prod_{i\in E}P_{d-e_i}\to P_d,\qquad (p_i)_{i\in E}\mapsto\sum_{i\in E}F_i\,p_i ,
--   $$
--   whose image is the degree-$d$ part $(F_i)_{i\in E}\cap P_d$ of the ideal generated by the $F_i$. A scalar multiple of a $w$-homogeneous polynomial of degree $d$ is again $w$-homogeneous of degree $d$.
--
--   With these notions the split bound of a list of factor pairs becomes the sum, over all choice vectors $c$, of $\operatorname{pd}\bigl(I+\text{choice ideal of }c,\ d-\text{choice shift of }c\bigr)$. For $m=\sum_ja_j$ products $\ell_{u(i)}(t_i)\,\ell_{v(i)}(t'_i)$ of Vandermonde block forms with all $2m$ parameters pairwise distinct, this bounds the dimension of the degree-$d$ piece of the quotient by these products by the coefficient of $X^{a}$ in $M_{u,v}$, as soon as every entry of $d$ exceeds $m$. Linear coefficient subspaces of codimension at most one, respectively zero, translate into proportionality relations among the selected variables modulo $I$, respectively into their membership in $I$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The definitions are `linearFormMap`, `linearCoefficientSubspace`, `BlockVariables` (a sigma type over `ι`), `blockVar`, `blockLinearForm`, `pieceDim`, `choiceIdeal`, `choiceShift`, `choiceCount` (a finitely supported function `ι →₀ ℕ`), `mixedPolynomial` (natural-number coefficients) and `homogeneousIdealMap`. Choice vectors are Boolean functions on `Fin qs.length`, with `true` selecting the right factor $b_k$. `pieceDim` is a `Module.finrank`, hence $0$ for infinite-dimensional spaces. The lemmas `linearFormMap_apply`, `blockLinearForm_homogeneous` and `isWeightedHomogeneous_smul` are the formula in item 1 and the homogeneity facts in items 4 and 8.
